al Africa. The genus Gorilla is divided into two species: the eastern gorilla and the western gorilla, and either four or five subspecies.","revisionId":1372671781,"title":"Gorilla","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gorilla","wikidataId":"Q36611"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Pelicans","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Pelican","source":"Martha's Vineyard species checklist"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Pelecanidae","confidence":94,"rank":"family","scientificName":"Pelecanidae","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":9329},"ottId":452465,"rank":"family","scientificName":"Pelecanidae","synonyms":[],"wikipedia":{"extract":"The Pelecanidae is a family of pelecaniform birds within the Pelecani that contains three genera: the extinct Eopelecanus and Miopelecanus and the extant Pelecanus. Pelecanids have existed since the late Eocene (Priabonian) and they still exist today.","revisionId":1314859369,"title":"Pelecanidae","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pelecanidae","wikidataId":"Q11846678"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Bearded Bee-eaters","source":"Catalogue of Life"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Nyctyornis","confidence":94,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Nyctyornis Jardine & Selby, 1830","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":2475457},"ottId":524017,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Nyctyornis","synonyms":["Nycthiornis","Nyctinomus","Nyctiornis"],"wikipedia":{"extract":"Nyctyornis is a genus of the bee-eaters, near passerine birds in the family Meropidae. There are just two members of this group, which occur in tropical south and southeastern Asia.","revisionId":1359457817,"title":"Nyctyornis","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nyctyornis","wikidataId":"Q285047"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Golden-bellied Mangabey","source":"The IUCN Red List of Threatened Species"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Cercocebus chrysogaster","confidence":99,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Cercocebus chrysogaster Lydekker, 1900","status":"ACCEPTED"